<title>BELGIUM: Belgian insurer Secura raises capital.</title>
<headline>Belgian insurer Secura raises capital.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian insurance firm Secura Belgian Re said it had struck a deal with two existing and two new shareholders to raise its share capital to 3.56 billion francs from 2.1 billion.</p>
<p>The two new shareholders, Dutch bank Rabobank unit Interpolis and British insurer NFU Mutual will each hold 20.83 percent of Secura.</p>
<p>Existing shareholders  ABB (Belgium) and  DVV (Belgium) hold 52.51 percent and 5.83 percent of Secura respectively.</p>
<p>Secura's premium income this year is estimated at 4.2 billion francs.</p>
